     3	/**
     4	 * A claim's status: it starts as DRAFT, is opened (OPEN) and then settled (SETTLED); a clerk settling
     5	 * one above the clerk limit leaves it PENDING until a steward approves it (SETTLED) or rejects it (back to
     6	 * OPEN). A DRAFT, OPEN or PENDING claim can be voided (VOID), and a
     7	 * steward may void a SETTLED one within 7 days of its settlement. A DRAFT can be DELETED, and restored to a DRAFT on
     8	 * the sheet's today it was deleted. A claim whose due is above the sheet's review threshold goes to REVIEW
     9	 * instead of OPEN when opened, until a steward reviews it (OPEN); a REVIEW claim can be voided. Only OPEN,
    10	 * PENDING and SETTLED claims count toward what is claimed.
    11	 */
    12	public enum ClaimStatus {
    13	    DRAFT, OPEN, PENDING, SETTLED, VOID, DELETED, REVIEW;
    14	
    15	    /** Whether the claim counts toward claimed, due-total and every total. */
    16	    public boolean counts() {
    17	        return this == OPEN || this == PENDING || this == SETTLED;
    18	    }
    19	
    20	    /** Whether the claim is still to be paid: OPEN or PENDING. */
    21	    public boolean unpaid() {
    22	        return this == OPEN || this == PENDING;
    23	    }
    24	
    25	    /**
    26	     * Whether a claim in this status may be moved to the given one by opening, settling or voiding it; a
    27	     * PENDING claim leaves PENDING only by being approved, rejected or voided, and a REVIEW claim REVIEW only
    28	     * by being reviewed or voided.
    29	     */
    30	    public boolean canBecome(ClaimStatus next) {
    31	        return switch (next) {
    32	            case OPEN -> this == DRAFT;
    33	            case PENDING, SETTLED -> this == OPEN;
    34	            case VOID -> this == DRAFT || this == OPEN || this == PENDING || this == SETTLED || this == REVIEW;
    35	            case DRAFT, DELETED, REVIEW -> false;
    36	        };
    37	    }
    38	}
